de Valley/Eastern San Juan Mountains Below 10000 Ft; Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.928785af67df25edfd60d6c08af371547045920b.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.928785af67df25edfd60d6c08af371547045920b.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 31 at 9:18PM MDT until November 4 at 5:00AM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall will be possible,\nespecially over the western half of San Luis Valley.\n\n* WHERE...The western half of the San Luis Valley, including\nAntonito, Del Norte, Monte Vista and Alamosa.\n\n* WHEN...From Sunday afternoon through late Tuesday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone location.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Runoff from heavy rain and melting snow over the San Juan\nMountains may cause flooding in the San Luis Valley, especially\nMonday and Tuesday as high flows move out of the mountains and\nthrough the Rio Grande and Conejos River.\n- The greatest risk of flooding will be along the Conejos River and\nthe Rio Grande, including Del Norte, Monte Vista and Alamosa.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood http://cotrip.org","ends":"2026-11-04T05:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Del Norte Vicinity/Northern San Luis Valley Below 8500 Ft; Alamosa  Vicinity/Central San Luis Valley Below 8500 Ft; Southern San Luis Valley","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.928785af67df25edfd60d6c08af371547045920b.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.928785af67df25edfd60d6c08af371547045920b.002.1"},{"event":"Avalanche Advisory","headline":"Avalanche Advisory issued October 31 at 7:16PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"SABCO\n\nTHE FOLLOWING MESSAGE IS TRANSMITTED AT THE REQUEST OF THE\nCOLORADO AVALANCHE INFORMATION CENTER.\n\n...A SPECIAL AVALANCHE ADVISORY IN EFFECT FROM 4:30 PM SATURDAY\nUNTIL 4:30 PM MONDAY...\n\n*WHAT...Avalanche conditions are dangerous above treeline.\n*WHERE...West Elk Mountains, Elk Mountains, San Juan Mountains, and\nLa Plata Mountains\n*WHEN...From 4:30 PM Saturday until 4:30 PM Monday.\n*IMPACTS...Backcountry travelers can easily trigger dangerous\navalanches large enough to bury a human.\n\n*PRECAUTION/PREPAREDNESS ACTIONS...A potent winter storm increases\navalanche danger Sunday into Monday. Rain, snow, and wind will cause\nnatural avalanches above treeline. Check the forecast at\nwww.colorado.gov/avalanche.\n\nBeyer & Pritchett","ends":"2026-11-02T16:30:00-07:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"West Elk and Sawatch Mountains; Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5d9a0ec4f46df7deb3c2c0e5015df58147db243f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5d9a0ec4f46df7deb3c2c0e5015df58147db243f.001.1"},{"event":"Winter Storm Warning","headline":"Winter Storm Warning issued October 31 at 6:20PM MDT until November 2 at 11:00AM MST by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Heavy snow expected. Total snow accumulations 8 to 14\ninches. Winds gusting as high as 50 mph.\n\n* WHERE...Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Feet.\n\n* WHEN...From 5 PM Sunday to 11 AM MST Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be very difficult, especially Sunday night\nand Monday morning. Strong winds could produce areas of blowing and\ndrifting snow.","ends":"2026-11-02T11:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.681963bb8119fe118c9c03d331c7709ba2bd3b05.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.681963bb8119fe118c9c03d331c7709ba2bd3b05.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-11-01T07:04:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 010704 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 104 AM MDT Sun Nov 1 2026 .KEY MESSAGES